 Yes, you can store and manage binary data such as images in MongoDB using GridFS or the Binary Data Type. GridFS is a popular solution for storing large binary files like images in MongoDB. It divides the file into chunks and stores each chunk as a separate document in a collection. This makes it easier to handle large files compared to storing them directly as BSON objects.

To use GridFS, you need to install the `gridfs-stream` package if you're using Node.js or `pymongo-gridfs` if you're using Python. After setting up GridFS, you can save an image by writing its content to a write stream created by GridFS:

